WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.077 --> 00:00:01.658
-Good evening. I'm Seth Meyers.

00:00:01.658 --> 00:00:03.936
This is "Late Night."
We hope you had a great weekend.

00:00:03.936 --> 00:00:05.171
Let's get to the news.

00:00:05.171 --> 00:00:07.407
According to a new report,
President Biden is ready

00:00:07.407 --> 00:00:09.742
to help lobby moderate Democrats

00:00:09.742 --> 00:00:12.077
to support reforming
the filibuster

00:00:12.077 --> 00:00:14.747
and told Senate Majority Leader
Chuck Schumer,

00:00:14.747 --> 00:00:18.084
"Tell me when you need me
to start making phone calls."

00:00:18.084 --> 00:00:19.252
Said Schumer,

00:00:19.252 --> 00:00:22.588
"You haven't even started
making calls?!"

00:00:22.588 --> 00:00:25.424
During a speech on Thursday
outlining his new plan

00:00:25.424 --> 00:00:26.759
to fight the coronavirus,

00:00:26.759 --> 00:00:29.095
President Biden
scolded travelers

00:00:29.095 --> 00:00:31.263
who refuse to wear masks
on airplanes.

00:00:31.263 --> 00:00:34.433
Great. Now do shoes.

00:00:34.433 --> 00:00:37.436
During a September 11th
memorial dinner on Saturday,

00:00:37.436 --> 00:00:40.940
Rudy Giuliani imitated
Britain's Queen Elizabeth

00:00:40.940 --> 00:00:43.109
by marrying his cousin.

00:00:43.109 --> 00:00:46.279
[ Laughter ]

00:00:46.279 --> 00:00:48.614
Supreme Court Justice
Amy Coney Barrett

00:00:48.614 --> 00:00:49.949
appeared yesterday at an event

00:00:49.949 --> 00:00:51.784
with Senate Minority Leader
Mitch McConnell

00:00:51.784 --> 00:00:53.452
and said she was worried

00:00:53.452 --> 00:00:56.122
that the public sees the court
as a partisan institution,

00:00:56.122 --> 00:00:59.458
which is kind of like performing
at the VMAs with Taylor Swift

00:00:59.458 --> 00:01:02.795
and worrying that people will
see you as a musician.

00:01:02.795 --> 00:01:05.464
The MTV Music Awards --
Video Music Awards were held

00:01:05.464 --> 00:01:07.333
last night, and Madonna made
a surprise appearance

00:01:07.333 --> 00:01:09.668
to open the show.
The audience was so shocked,

00:01:09.668 --> 00:01:13.338
they all got out their phones
and looked her up on Wikipedia.

00:01:13.338 --> 00:01:15.341
I know. They're young.

00:01:15.341 --> 00:01:17.209
I know.

00:01:17.209 --> 00:01:19.879
The fast food chain Burger King
last week unveiled

00:01:19.879 --> 00:01:22.047
its so-called Keep It Real Meal,

00:01:22.047 --> 00:01:24.216
which partners with
several celebrities,

00:01:24.216 --> 00:01:26.886
but uses their real names
instead of stage names.

00:01:26.886 --> 00:01:28.554
Though I'm not sure how well

00:01:28.554 --> 00:01:31.891
the Robert Allen Zimmerman
burger will sell.

00:01:31.891 --> 00:01:33.726
[ Laughter ]

00:01:33.726 --> 00:01:35.894
An investigation concluded
last week

00:01:35.894 --> 00:01:40.532
that a recent MTA subway outage
that shut down 83 trains

00:01:40.532 --> 00:01:41.701
was caused by someone

00:01:41.701 --> 00:01:43.869
accidentally flipping
a power switch.

00:01:43.869 --> 00:01:45.037
Said one man,

00:01:45.037 --> 00:01:47.873
"So that's what it does!"

00:01:47.873 --> 00:01:49.908
And finally,
Facebook has collaborated

00:01:49.908 --> 00:01:52.745
with the eyewear brand Ray-Ban
to release new sunglasses

00:01:52.745 --> 00:01:55.848
that can take pictures, make
phone calls, and play music.

00:01:55.848 --> 00:01:57.182
On the downside,

00:01:57.182 --> 00:01:58.852
you're currently
sitting on them.

00:01:58.852 --> 00:02:00.220
And that was the monologue.

